    "title": "Mercedes Mone Aligns With Divine Dominion - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ryan Clark ,\n21 minutes ago\nMercedes Mone appears to have found some powerful new allies in AEW.\nDuring the closing moments of the Women’s Casino Gauntlet Match on this week’s episode of AEW Dynamite: Beach Break, a major alliance was revealed. After the match, AEW Women’s Tag Team Champions Divine Dominion, Megan Bayne and Lena Kross, stormed the entrance ramp and laid out Julia Hart and Skye Blue.\nMoments later, Mone joined the chaos by attacking both Thekla and Willow Nightingale inside the ring, leaving the competition down as the numbers game took over.\nREAD MORE: WWE Star Praises AEW Wrestler For Transitioning Himself\nREAD MORE: Tony Khan Explains AEW’s Title Match TV Strategy, Nick Offerman Lands Emmy Nomination\nWith the dust settled, Mone stood alongside Bayne and Kross, confirming that she has officially aligned herself with Divine Dominion in what appears to be a new business arrangement.\nThe trio closed the segment by posing together, signaling that one of AEW’s most dominant forces has grown even stronger.\nDivine Dominion have held the AEW Women’s Tag Team Championships since March, when they defeated the Babes of Wrath, Harley Cameron and Willow Nightingale, to capture the titles.\nNOTE: If you have any news tips or podcast recaps that you’d like to send in for us to post (full credit will be given to you), please email me at RClarkPWS@Yahoo.com .",
    "summary": "During the closing moments of the Women’s Casino Gauntlet Match on this week’s episode of AEW Dynamite: Beach Break, a major alliance was revealed. After the match, AEW Women’s Tag Team Champions Divine Dominion, Megan Bayne and Lena Kross, stormed the entrance ramp and laid out Julia Hart and Skye Blue. Moments later, Mone joined the chaos by attacking both Thekla and Willow Nightingale inside the ring, leaving the competition down as the numbers game took over.",
